Z||000004||spike||05-14-99||07:05 AM||||I had an 87 gt about 2 years ago. One of my headlights suddenly stopped in the up position a couple of times. I raised the front hood and turned the little black knob that if I remember right is on the side of the headlight. I would close the lights and turn this knob a little and it would suddenly go down. I am not sure if this will work for you but it has always for me. I am not sure what this knob is for, but it cured my problems.
Z||000005||Carrolles||05-14-99||07:39 AM||||I have the Helms manula for my 85se.  It has all of the wiring diagrams (schematics) as well as the wiring layout sketches.  It also has an excellent troubleshooting procedure.<br>You said that you just leave the headlights up.  How do you get them up in the first place?  Do you use the manual lift knob to crank it up?<br>There are actually three relays that control the headlights.  A sort of master relay and one isolation relay for each light.  I believe they are all near the left headlight housing.<br>I'd be glad to scan the charts and e-mail them to you if you'd like.  I usually get home on weekends (I work in St. Louis and live in Birmingham, AL).<br>Let me know.<br>Good luck,<br>Carroll
Z||000006||EMF||05-14-99||04:12 PM||||just buy a  new motor, and use them very very little.  
Z||000007||ezsurf||05-14-99||06:34 PM||||Spike,<br>The black knob is for manually raising and lowering the headlight in case the motor or relay fails, so you can still drive at night.  I used to have a Toyota Supra that was the same way.  It also had a position on the headlight switch that would allow you to raise your headlights, but leave the lights off.  This was for winter time so that snow and ice build up wouldn't freeze your headlights in the down position.  If you tried to raise them when their frozen shut, you would damage the gear mechanism or motor.
Z||000008||burdell1||05-14-99||11:54 PM||||Carroll,<p>That would be great if you could send me a copy of the layout sketches for the wiring.  I would really appreciate it. My e-mail address is burdell1@yahoo.com. Thanks<p>
